A||N||15||Voytek||Dumb Mechanics and Fieros - any experience?||||10||
Z||000000||Voytek||06-01-2001||03:50 PM||||This topic may have been covered dozens of times, but here are my experiences.<BR>1.  Went to Crappy Tire a while back with my '85 4-cyl (that's Canadian Tire to Americans).  So I'm standing in the parking lot and watching this.  First, the mechanic gets inside the car.  One minute, two minutes....  I walk up and say: 'are you looking for the e-brake?'  He nods.  I show him where it is and walk away.  One minute, two minutes... The car starts, the brake lights come on.  By now the suspense is killing me.  The engine revs but the car is not backing up (??).  It starts rolling forward (!!) and hits a van in front!!!  Phew, I think to myself.  Good thing that van was there or who knows HOW far this guy would have rolled.  I was shaken up but otherwise OK.<BR>2.  Crappy Tire again.  This was the second and last experience with them (I haven't been there since).  So I drop off my '85 4-cyl for an alignment one beautiful Saturday.  About 4 hours later I call to find out if it's done.  The answer is 'no, and it won't be.  Your car is too low'.  WHAT TH' ??!!  I hop in another car and get my ass over there pronto.  I say to the foreman (or some dude whose forehead looked a bit taller than the rest of the 'mechanics') 'what do you mean you won't work on my car?'.  He says 'your car is too low'.  I say 'this car is all stock.  What do you mean it's too low?'  Reply: 'we can't get it up the ramps.  It's too low.'  As I pop a vain in my forehead, I try to remain calm and say: 'have you even tried getting it up the ramps?  I mean, no one else has had a prblem until now.'  To which the bright gentleman says 'no, we haven't tried.  Our mechanic can eye-ball pretty good'.  (????!!!!!!!!).  This is the part where I lose my nerve.  I leave the shop telling him to put a big sign in the window ' WE DON'T WORK ON FIEROS.<BR>3.  I needed the oil pan gasket replaced on my '87 GT (in the days before I started doing stuff like this myself).  So I made an appointment with a local shop (Blaskin And Lane).  I drop off the car and am told that it will be ready in a couple of hours.  A couple of hours later I call to see if it's ready.  The answer?  'No, it's not.  In fact, we have decided not to work on it because it's a Fiero'.  You can imagine how fast I drove down to that place.  The explaination?  'Our mechanic feels uncomfortable working on this car'.  Maybe your mechanic needs some Preperation H?!!  So I tell him 'but this is a GM 2.8, just like any other GM 2.8, only in the back'.  The answer: 'still, it's differenct enough that we will not work on it.<BR>Maybe they should just stick to working on bicycles.<BR>These are my Fiero-related, bad-mechanic stories.  Anyone have some good ones?||||reg||10
Z||000001||Neal||06-01-2001||05:31 PM||||Now i take offence to the bicycle mechanic crack Voytek.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||06-01-2001||05:47 PM||||On 2 different occasions a mechanic broke the fuel door release lever thinking it was the rear deck release. Of course, I didn't know about 'till it was time to refill a few days later...<P>Another time, I wound up with a cracked GT sail panel because of a mechanic leaning on it too heavily.  It was tinted, so I didn't even notice until a couple weeks later.<P>I try to do ALL my own work.  When needed, I take my car to Mikkelson's AC Delco and have their mechanic who owned a Fiero work on it. No problems there.  I've never had a problem getting an alignment at Harper's Tire - even with the car lowered.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Toddster||06-01-2001||05:54 PM||||I went into a Grand Auto Parts and asked for an, "upper engine gasket set for a Pontiac Fiero with a 2.8 Liter V-6 engine with A/C".<P>The "kid" behind the counter asked if that was a truck. I replied, "I'm outta here".<P>The average garage monkey today was in diapers when they stopped making the Fiero so the lesson is go to a mechanic over 30 years of age or do it yourself!||||reg||1
Z||000004||FLASHY||06-01-2001||06:05 PM||||When I needed to get a wheel alignment after lowering the fiero (cut the coils) I phoned around to see who would do it. EVERYBODY didn't want to do it. They either criticized me because "who lowers a fiero???" or they said "NOPE, you screwed up everything now, it can't be done". WTF is up with that? Like it's really any different than any other lowered car. Crappy Tire told me the same thing Voytek, "Fiero's can't get on the ramp, especially once it's lowered." Even though I've had my fiero on their ramp before. Finally Fountain Tire said they'd look at the car and see if they can do it. Well, the mechanic said, "Of course it can be done. Why not?" And he did it!!!....BUT...he forgot to make sure the coils were seated down on the strut properly when putting the car back down on the wheels. After I picked up my car, I notice it's not sitting level so I look underneath and find the coils resting on the wheel well!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  So I took it back and he fixed it. You always have to wonder if your fiero will actually come out of a shop in better shape than when you dropped it off there.<P>There, I feel better now.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flashy_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||8
Z||000005||banditbalz||06-01-2001||07:11 PM||||My GT has NEVER come back from a mechanic without having something broken or not working properly. The worst one was 4 years ago, I had the local G.M. dealership replace my clutch, transmission and engine mounts. Total charge was in the neighbourhood of $3000 Canadian. Upon changing my oil later that week, I discovered that both the rear tranny mount AND the main rear engine mount had no freakin' nuts on the bolts. it was only the weight of the engine holding it in place. What a shop full of dumbasses... i replaced the nuts myself for fear they would screw something else up...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||13
Z||000006||Jay||06-01-2001||07:15 PM||||I will never take my car to Canadian Tire. It's full of learning students who wern't even born when the Fiero was made!  One guy brought his car to Canadian Tire to have the tranny done on it.  A few days later they told him to come pick the car up.  When he arrived it was in pieces.  The engine was out, the tranny was out, suspension dropped.  They said "We wont work on it anymore, it's too complicated!"  And they made him pay for the labour in removing the engine!  He called a flat bed and had it towed to Race-Tech (The Fiero Shop) in Toronto.  Then he threatened to sue Canadian Tire and they paid for the work and the damage they caused to his car.  <P>From now on, I do the work myself or take it to Race-Tech.  That's it, no Yahoo is going to touch my car.  I wouldn't even take a Lada to them!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kick.gif">  <BR>THE NORTHSTAR GIVES YOU A REAL KICK IN THE ASS!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Urchin||06-01-2001||07:25 PM||||I had to replace my engine awhile back.  I couldn't afford a rebuild so I took it to a shop where the guy I normally deal with is a fellow fiero enthusiast.  I figured it was in good hands.  I come in two days later to check on how things are going, and the guy that I had left my car with took a sick leave for 2 months.  I thought uh oh, this is going to be trouble.  To make a really long story shorter, I had it back (with warrenty in hand) 4 times!  Let me rephrase that, I had it towed back 4 times!  Various problems which are irrelevant.  So once I get it back with a decent running engine in it I discovered that they didn't swap all the parts from my old engine.  I had just put in new plugs/wires, distributer (all components), starter, the list goes on.  Point being, I had to redo all of that work all over again.  I took it back, and they were sick of seeing me by then and would not own up to just throwing in the other engine without swaping my parts over, as previously agreed.   I'm glad it's overwith!<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_8.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||06-01-2001||08:09 PM||||I dropped my Fiero off for a tune up, and a new clutch. 11 months later I got my car back. Tuneup sucked, the car came back with a overheating problem it didnt have before. The gear shifter linkages came back out of adjustment, blocky and stiff compared to how smooth they was. They broke both my front sidemarker lights then expected me to pay for their screw up. And I have just found out now, a year later that the idiots have removed my lower left engine mount and just left it out. Wondered why the car was kicking one way on  take off.<P>I have been to 2 mechanics since and both are idiots when it comes to Fieros. The car has come back worse each time yet they still have the nerve to charge for their time.<P>Perhaps I should just build non functioning web sites and charge my customers because, it took a lot of time to stuff it up that good.<P>For any other Australians out there do not use Joes Mechanical Repairs in Wollongong as the guy is an idiot who will only stuff your car.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||9
Z||000009||Jefrysuko||06-02-2001||01:13 AM||||The only thing I have taken a fiero to the shop for is an allignment and luckily noone has screwed it up to much.  The one I hate to hear is when someone uses a lift with the arms and puts them right under the coolant pipes.  I saw pictures once where the guy wasn't paying attention and the car fell off half way up in the air.<P>What do you mean I can't lift it like that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||lowCG||06-02-2001||02:12 AM||||I have to agree with the "alignment only" rule.<BR>I looked at my car when it was on a lift getting new tires,and noticed that the flip-up stands were't even touching the car's frame sections! The whole car was being supported by the floor panels;good thing it didn't start to rotate and fall off.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||SteveJ||06-02-2001||10:17 AM||||Took mine in for a state inspection to one of those quick change oil places and they refused to do it saying the district manager told them no Fieros. I argued. They numbled something about low clearance and liability. I bet there was a law suit about this and it hit one of their trade magasines and that's why some places are hesitant.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Voytek2||06-02-2001||07:48 PM||||Not another Voytek!!<BR>Oh, wait a minute, the other name is mine too...  (just had to register from another computer).<P>Ok.  I have one more story (I've had more mechanic screw-ups than I can count).<BR>As some of you know, about 2 months ago I had my 2.8 rebuilt into a 3.1.  After picking up the car, I noticed that the power mirror switch was missing (just the top button).  I went back to ask if they knew where it was.  'duuuh, we have no idea what you're talking about' was the reply.  I thought 'fine, whatever, I'll find a new switch'.  Well, it didin't stop there.  I also noticed that the lighter socket just wasn't fitting properly.  Being too lazy to take it out and see what's wrong, I waited until about 2 weeks ago to take the center console apart at the same time as I was re-wiring the speakers in my Fiero.  When I took out the console, I realized that the lighter socket will NEVER fit properly again because the BASTARDS broke the platic (that holds the console together) into many little pieces!!!  How th' hell do you do that?  Did they have it sitting on the ground and drop the engine on it???  And the thing is, two months later I can't go back and complain 'cause they'll say that I did this.  What a bunch of fu*king morons!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Her86GT||06-02-2001||09:03 PM||||I took my 86GT to my mechanic and asked him to put two Sunfire seats in that I got from the wreckers.  He handed me his impact gun and a few sockets and said for me to go at it.  Shocked, I said "Sure - whatever - I can do this".  So I did.  Looks great.||||reg||12
Z||000014||thomas_l||06-03-2001||10:08 AM||||Two things I don't do myself: alignments and exhaust work. For alignments I use the Tire Force in Alpharetta. I knew they were good from my first visit. Since then I have heard them mentioned alot at SCCA SOLO-II events and Porsche club members. They did my 87 GT with no BS and at the regular price. I got my catalytic convertor done at a Mighty Muffler in Duluth on the recommendation of a neighbor. They also installed a new right-rear hanger. The first attempt resulted in a rattle and some leakage at one of the welds. I took it back in and was back out in an hour everything OK. Later, the left-rear hanger broke. I went back in and they popped one in for $10.<P>Just thought I would brag about some good service in my neighborhood  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000015||Fiero Sam||06-03-2001||11:35 AM||||I took my 87 Coupe in for a tune-up(up until recently,the only thing I knew about cars is where you keep the tires,hey,I would make a great mechanic!).<BR>I went back about a week later(they are real slow but usually pretty good)and she sounded like she was about to die.She sounded alot better than that when I took her in.This older mechanic comes out and says"What's wrong with it?"<BR>I wanted to punch him right in the mouth.<BR>Finally,the mechanic who works on my car comes out.<BR>He did not adjust the gap on one of the spark plugs properly.<BR>He was supposed to be off work then,but he stayed and fixed it for me.<BR>This is the only trouble I have ever had with them and they are pretty honest.<BR>I have tried to get my car painted there twice.They said they would call me when they have an opening but they never did.I got her painted somewhere else.<BR>||||reg||1
